WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.444
Hi Marcus,

2
00:00:02.445 --> 00:00:06.918
I hope you like your new school, but I really miss you here!

3
00:00:06.935 --> 00:00:12.853
This year the drama club is putting on William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet

4
00:00:12.854 --> 00:00:18.751
. You probably think I'm playing Romeo since I'm usually the lead in drama club

5
00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:21.516
productions. But you're

6
00:00:21.517 --> 00:00:23.936
wrong. I'm not even in the

7
00:00:23.937 --> 00:00:28.093
cast! Mrs. Geller picked me for stage

8
00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:34.121
manager. I'll be in charge of the sets, sound and lighting, and

9
00:00:34.122 --> 00:00:39.589
props. She said it would be good experience, but it sounds pretty boring to me.

10
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.579
And you know what makes it even worse?

11
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:47.344
Rose Adams is playing Juliet!

12
00:00:47.345 --> 00:00:51.498
This would have been my chance to get to know her better.

13
00:00:51.499 --> 00:00:56.908
Instead I'm stuck backstage, and Jae gets to be Romeo.

14
00:00:56.909 --> 00:01:00.470
I guess it's good that you moved all the way across the country.

15
00:01:00.471 --> 00:01:03.455
Things around here aren't much fun.

16
00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:06.214
Hope to hear from you soon!

17
00:01:06.215 --> 00:01:12.138
Carlos

18
00:01:12.139 --> 00:01:13.367
***

19
00:01:13.368 --> 00:01:16.077
Hey! Sorry it's been so long since I

20
00:01:16.078 --> 00:01:18.160
wrote. I've been super

21
00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:21.457
busy! The sets for the play are supposed to be pretty

22
00:01:21.458 --> 00:01:25.791
basic. But we've been working every single afternoon to build what we

23
00:01:25.792 --> 00:01:32.773
need. We just finished the set for the scene where Juliet talks to Romeo from her

24
00:01:32.774 --> 00:01:36.847
balcony. I came up with the idea for the

25
00:01:36.848 --> 00:01:42.960
set. We painted big pieces of cardboard to look like the front of Juliet's

26
00:01:42.961 --> 00:01:50.283
house. Then we cut out a doorway and added a

27
00:01:50.284 --> 00:01:54.813
railing. Rose stands on a platform behind the cardboard front.

28
00:01:54.814 --> 00:02:00.545
It looks just like she's looking over a balcony railing!

29
00:02:00.546 --> 00:02:04.871
We're making props too.

30
00:02:04.872 --> 00:02:11.369
We used wood for daggers and painted the blades with shiny silver paint.

31
00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:17.688
Jae's little brother lent us a giant plastic baseball bat.

32
00:02:17.689 --> 00:02:24.027
We covered it with brown paper to make it look like a wooden club for the fight scene in act 1.

33
00:02:24.028 --> 00:02:31.359
It's actually fun thinking of ways to make things or adapt them to look realistic for the props.

34
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.182
I have to run now.

35
00:02:33.183 --> 00:02:36.834
We're meeting in a few minutes to discuss sound and lighting.

36
00:02:36.835 --> 00:02:38.100
Talk to you soon!

37
00:02:38.101 --> 00:02:41.083
Carlos

38
00:02:41.084 --> 00:02:45.127
*** I don't know how we're going to get everything done in two

39
00:02:45.128 --> 00:02:51.674
weeks! The cast is rehearsing every afternoon, and the backstage crew is working long hours

40
00:02:51.675 --> 00:02:58.551
too. If we don't get the sets, lighting, and sound just right, the play will be

41
00:02:58.552 --> 00:03:04.518
ruined. I've learned how to set up the sound system so even people in the rear of the theater can hear everything.

42
00:03:04.519 --> 00:03:09.307
If there wasn't a sound system, the actors would need to yell!

43
00:03:09.308 --> 00:03:12.404
Lighting is tricky too.

44
00:03:12.405 --> 00:03:17.820
Without it, the audience wouldn't be able to see much onstage.

45
00:03:17.821 --> 00:03:22.722
You have to aim the light where the action is.

46
00:03:22.723 --> 00:03:28.237
It's taken some practice to make sure we move the lights up and down on cue.

47
00:03:28.238 --> 00:03:35.571
And you're not going to believe this: Jae broke his leg playing soccer, so he's out of the play!

48
00:03:35.572 --> 00:03:42.536
Mrs. Geller asked me to replace him since I've been helping him with his lines and know almost all of them.

49
00:03:42.537 --> 00:03:47.349
But I've just gotten the hang of working the sound system.

50
00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:52.854
Working backstage is more fun than I thought, and there's still a lot to do.

51
00:03:52.855 --> 00:04:03.338
We have to design and print programs, put up posters to advertise the play, and take care of so many more details.

52
00:04:03.339 --> 00:04:08.927
Luckily Mrs. Geller said Larry could play Romeo if I help him practice.

53
00:04:08.928 --> 00:04:11.492
Whew! Thank you, Larry! Carlos

54
00:04:11.493 --> 00:04:16.123
***

55
00:04:16.124 --> 00:04:18.433
Hey Marcus!

56
00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:20.907
Too bad you couldn't come!

57
00:04:20.908 --> 00:04:24.150
The play sold out and the audience loved it.

58
00:04:24.151 --> 00:04:28.166
I think this is our best drama club production ever.

59
00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:33.082
We still have six more performances and they're all sold out.

60
00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:37.480
I hope I get to work backstage again next year.

61
00:04:37.481 --> 00:04:41.383
Well, I have to rush off to the after-play party.

62
00:04:41.384 --> 00:04:48.580
I was talking to Juliet/Rose between scenes, and she said she hoped to see me there.

63
00:04:48.581 --> 00:04:54.204
Just call me backstage Romeo!

